## 2. Qualified claims (retained with footnote caveats)

### 2.1 51 Flagship Suites on AA 787-9P
Trade-press sourced (premium-flights.com, not AA primary). Directional; not load-bearing to recommendations. Retained with existing footnote caveat in [^6].

### 2.2 Connecting share (60%/two-thirds)
Neither figure has a primary AA document. Correctly disclosed in footnote [^22]. The design-basis midpoint (62.5%) is an analysis construct.

### 2.3 Rent range $100–150/sf/yr
Industry estimate for comparable non-signatory terminal space; no DFW-specific rate is in the evidence. Footnote [^17] retains the "order-of-magnitude" qualifier.

### 2.4 CPE behavioral threshold ~$20–22
Airline-commercial professional judgment; no peer-reviewed or primary source. Retained in the body as professional judgment; footnote [^51] discloses this.

### 2.5 DTW McNamara cost and retrofit history
"Without material retrofit" characterization comes from trade press and aviation enthusiast archives, not audited cost records. Footnote [^7] carries this qualification.

### 2.6 At-grade retrofit range ($204M–$600M)
Derived from analysis of at-grade lounge retrofit displacement cost. Methodology described in footnote [^58].

### 2.7 Decision card cost estimates (footnotes [^52], [^55]–[^59], [^61])
Engineering and program estimates for decision card costs (Cards 1–6); no independent cost audits exist in the public record. Footnotes document basis and limitations for each cost range.

### 2.8 O&M reserve 1.5% benchmark (footnote [^54])
Industry practice benchmark; applies broadly to large complex terminal facilities per ACRP research. Footnote [^54] discloses the professional-judgment basis.

### 2.9 Hub survival list (footnote [^32])
Historical analysis of US hub carrier retention through 2001–2015 consolidation wave. New record CL-075 added in post-gate pass. The specific list of 11 airports is a council analytical synthesis; individual outcomes are verifiable from public carrier histories.

### 2.10 DFW AA share 82.6% (footnote [^33])
Consistent with publicly available DFW statistics aggregators but previously attached evidence was an internal context packet (removed in post-gate remediation). Retained as qualified; footnote labels source as "secondary aggregation."

### 2.11 DFW Board governance (footnote [^40])
DFW board governance is public information but the primary source (city ordinances/bylaws) was not re-fetched during this remediation pass. Evidence from internal context packet removed; retained as qualified.

### 2.12 Governance threshold $10M (footnote [^39])
Policy design choice established by this analysis as a governance judgment. Not derived from an external standard or published benchmark. New record CL-074 added in post-gate pass.

